title: PlatformZero_Setup
---
<<declare $pz_quest_started = false>>
<<declare $pz_has_notebook = false>>
<<declare $pz_notebook_returned = false>>
<<declare $pz_story_complete = false>>
<<declare $pz_ended = false>>
===

title: Nina
---
<<if $pz_story_complete>>
    <<jump Nina_done>>
<<elseif $pz_notebook_returned>>
    <<jump Nina_reveal>>
<<elseif $pz_has_notebook>>
    <<jump Nina_quest_completed>>
<<elseif $pz_quest_started>>
    <<jump Nina_quest_started>>
<<else>>
    <<jump Nina_begin>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Nina_begin
---
Nina: Front pocket, main compartment, bench. I've checked all three. Repeating the same procedure isn't going to...
Nina: Unless I missed the lining. Shit. Start again.
Player: What're we looking for?
Nina: A red notebook. I put it beside me before checking the timetable. Objects don't relocate themselves, so clearly I've missed something.
Player: Mmmmmmmmm. Red one.
Nina: Check the far benches. Underneath, not just around them. And don't open it. There's a loose sheet inside.
Player: Evan's thing?
Nina: His chemistry notes, yes. I rewrote them because mine had annotations. It would have been confusing.
Player: Awwwww. You made him a nice copy.
Nina: A legible copy. That's a fairly basic courtesy.
Player: Little headings and everything.
Nina: Could you look for it, please?
<<set $pz_quest_started = true>>
===

title: Nina_quest_started
---
Nina: Did you check the gap beneath the backrest? You need to bend down. Looking at the bench from standing height accomplishes very little.
Player: Was getting there.
Nina: You were looking at the vending machine.
Player: It's got soup.
Nina: Please.
===

title: Notebook
---
<<if $pz_notebook_returned or $pz_has_notebook>>
    <<stop>>
<<elseif not $pz_quest_started>>
    Player: Huh. Better ask her.
<<else>>
    Player: There you are.
    <<set $pz_has_notebook = true>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Nina_quest_completed
---
Nina: Thank God. Wait, the elastic's loose. Did the separate sheet fall out? It should be folded once, writing facing inward.
Player: Still there.
<<set $pz_has_notebook = false>>
<<set $pz_notebook_returned = true>>
Nina: Right. Good. Except now the corner's bent. I can't give him that.
Player: Think he's gonna grade it?
Nina: No. We're studying together on Thursday. I'd simply prefer not to arrive with something crumpled.
Player: Mmmmmmmmmmmmm. Studying.
Nina: We are. His friends can't come, so it'll just be the two of us. That's hardly my fault.
Player:  Oh no.
Nina: What?
Player: All alone. With your diagrams.
Nina: You make it sound disgusting.
Player: Chemistry.
<<jump Nina_reveal>>
===

title: Nina_reveal
---
Nina: I've lost forty minutes. My report's unfinished, the group slides are incorrect, and now this needs rewriting. I had a perfectly workable schedule.
Player: Keep the sheet. It's fine.
Nina: It isn't fine. You can see the crease.
Player: Yeah. I see it.
Nina: Then why would you...
Player: Still says chemistry.
Nina: Do you approach your university assignments like this?
Player: When I open them.
Nina: God. I couldn't. I'd lie awake thinking about everything I'd done incorrectly.
Player: Right, three in the morning. Redoing the title.
Nina: Well, if the title's wrong.
Player: Mm.
Nina: I need to leave. Where do those stairs go?
Player: Back here.
Nina: That's impossible. Did you try the other side? There must be a different entrance or a staff passage. Someone needs to actually check.
Player: Probably.
Nina: Stop agreeing with me and help.
-> "Yeah. Okay."
    Player: Yeah. Okay.
    Nina: Thank you. Start with the door. I'll check whether there's an emergency number.
    Player: By the way, I just agreed with you again. :3 
-> "Here. Give me the bag."
    Player: Here. Give me the bag.
    Nina: Why?
    Player: You've opened it like six times.
    Nina: ...Don't put it on the floor.
Nina: I did everything early today. Everything. I don't understand what I'm supposed to correct.
Player: Dunno. I think we're just stuck.
<<set $pz_story_complete = true>>
===

title: Nina_done
---
Nina: Phone, notebook, keys. That's everything. I know that's everything.
Player: Little pocket's zipped.
Nina: Right. Let's go before I check again.
===

title: StationMap
---
Player: Huh.
Player: That's a lot of lines going nowhere.
===

title: StationExit
---
<<if not $pz_story_complete>>
    Player: Nope. Locked.
<<else>>
    Nina: It's open. Are you coming?
    Player: Yeah. Sorry. That light's been buzzing this whole time.
    Nina: ...Can I ask you something?
    Player: Mm?
    Nina: Do we get into our first choice?
    Player: Second.
    Nina: Oh.
    Player: There's a place near campus. Does these huge fries.
    Player: Second.
    Nina: Oh.
    Player: There's a place near campus. Huge fries.
    Nina: That's not really an equivalent outcome.
    Player: They put hamburger patties on them.
    Nina: I heard you.
    Nina: ...Do we like it there?
    Player: Yeah. Mostly.
    Nina: Okay. That's... okay.
    Player: Coming?
    Nina: Yes. And I'm keeping the sheet. He can read around the crease.
    Player: Alright, girl.
    Nina: Don't make it weird.
    Player: Wouldn't dream of it.
    <<set $pz_ended = true>>
<<endif>>
===